{"name":"Gristmill","hex":"#a29371","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"gristmill","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A mill that grinds grain; especially, a small-scale local mill that grinds grain brought by a local farmer to be exchanged for the resulting flour (less a percentage)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gristmill"}],"entries":[{"title":"Gristmill","blocks":[{"text":"A gristmill grinds cereal grain into flour and middlings. The term can refer to either the grinding mechanism or the building that holds it. Grist is grain that has been separated from its chaff in preparation for grinding."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/52/Allied_Mills%2C_Manchester.jpg/330px-Allied_Mills%2C_Manchester.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gristmill","wikidata":"Q623605"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/b/b0/Senenu_Grinding_Grain%2C_ca._1352-1336_B.C..jpg/500px-Senenu_Grinding_Grain%2C_ca._1352-1336_B.C..jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/b/b0/Senenu_Grinding_Grain%2C_ca._1352-1336_B.C..jpg/500px-Senenu_Grinding_Grain%2C_ca._1352-1336_B.C..jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Senenu Grinding Grain, c. 1352–1336 BC. The royal scribe Senenu appears here bent over a large grinding stone. This unusual sculpture seems to be an elaborate version of a shabti, a funerary figurine placed in the tomb to work in place of the deceased. Brooklyn Museum.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASenenu_Grinding_Grain%2C_ca._1352-1336_B.C..jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/10/Millstone_Anatomy.jpg/500px-Millstone_Anatomy.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.